hello everybody i'm grace vinod  raja from nishi sri lanka currently  studying bioprocess informatics  at the university of weinstefan tristoff  in bayern germany  and i have a basic background in medical  biology from the university of tuisburg  essen  as a final project of the program  bioinformatics for infectious diseases  by pine bio i have chosen the topic  human bronchial organized  a 3d in vitro test model for sas  coronavirus 2.  today i would like to present our  project and the finding from our study  the influence of different human  reference genome in rna sequence  analysis  and their impact on an in vitro kovic 19  drug test with chemostat  it is a joint project with mr priyanka  silachami  also known as victor from our course  even though my partner prepared some  interesting slides about the biological  background regarding  sas coronavirus 2 he couldn't able to  present his part of the project  since he got busy with his thesis works  so let me cover the theoretical part of  our project briefly  and let me get into the technical part  which i was mainly involved in  we all know about the impact of sas  coronavirus 2  around this world and we discussed  enough about spike proteins and as2  receptor  in our cell membrane  in our project we observed tmprss2  which is transmembrane serine protease  subtype  2 which play an important role  in activating the spike proteins  according to the scientists  of the german primate center also  known as deutsches primaten syndrome  once the spike proteins get activated  the virion could attach to  our as2 receptors in cell membrane  to avoid the activation of spike protein  we are going to study about  tmprss2 and chemostat  which is also known as tmprss2  inhibitors  chemostat is approved drug in japan  which is widely used  for pancreatic inflammation  as an innovative atom by a japanese  research institute of  microbial diseases they generated human  bronchial organize out of human  bronchial epithelial cells  furthermore they applied it as a test  model for their studies  moreover in human bronchial organize  they were able to observe different cell  types  which are significant for their studies  as well as  histologically significant for any  alveolar  or bronchial tissues  such as basal cells club cells  ciliated cells and goblet cells  for our research we performed ngs  analysis  on collected sra data from their studies  which is also available in ncbi as  open resource and we conducted a study  about the differential gene  expressions using both human reference  genomes  grch37 and grch38  these are the sra data which we  collected from ncbi  and we divided them into two groups in  the first proba set  we grouped a 549 cell clients  human bronchial epithelial cells and  human bronchial organized  to study about the similarity between  the cell types  in the second probe we grouped control  human bronchial organites  which were not infected sas coronavirus  ii  contaminated human bronchial organites  and sas coronavirus contaminated and  with chemostat treated human bronchial  organize  coming next to our problem statements  so we wanted to study about the impact  of different  reference genomes grch37 and 38  throughout our analysis  a differential gene expression studies  among the control  infected and treated human bronchial  organize  a control test to analyze contamination  of our probe too  as mentioned different pipelines of  transcriptomics  analysis were performed using both human  reference genomes separately  so grch37 and grch38  for each sets of probes  then the gene expression table were  quantile normalized  then a principal component analysis was  performed to study  the gene expression similarity within  the groups  in each proba set  the differential gene expression  analysis was performed  within each type of sample  in group two in probe one  it was only performed between human  bronchial epithelial cells  and human bronchial organize  finally we plotted the differential gene  expressions  on the available pathway diagrams  to precisely investigate the influence  of the reference genomes as a meta  genomic part of our study  a metagenomic microbiome analysis  pipeline was performed using all viruses  as a reference genome then the read  count of  different virus genome were obtained  from the pipeline output file  and the rate of all the coronavirus  genome were extracted out of the table  and annotated with the help of excel  tableau  and ncbi viral genome list  we performed a lot of pipelines but only  important results out of our  investigation  will be discussed here  from our analysis report of provost 1 we  were able to get results  from different transcriptomic pipelines  and  the results were identical in both grch  38  and grch37 we could observe a clear  grouping  in our principal component analysis  report as well  at the same time organized are more  alike to  human bronchial epithelial cells  comparing with  a549 cell lines  in our differential gene expression  analysis we did not observe any  significant differences  which was influenced by the reference  genome  dendrogram of our heat maps looks  identical in both human reference  genomes  and there is neither major different was  observed in volcano plot  moving on to the cake pathways we were  able to  observe additional differential gene  expressions  for grch38 in steroid hormone  biosynthesis pathway  and hematopoietic cell lineage pathway  as next moving into the second probe  we had issue performing transcriptomic  pipelines with their preference  genome grch38 although  with the grch37 we were able to obtain  resource  we were not able to conclude anything  about the quality of our  pro or pipeline errors since we were  able to get results for the grch37  moreover we had results for provo one  for both grch37  and 38 then a transcriptomic analysis  pipeline using sailfish method was  performed  without any preprocessing to get the  read table without any errors  in our principle component analysis we  were not able to  observe a clear grouping as we observed  in provo one  then we decided to do a batch correction  however we were convinced to continue  without batch correction as the scatter  plot  after batch correction looks so  artificial  we could see a clear separation between  control organized  and contaminated organoids although  there is no significant separation  observed  between infected and treated organoids  we proceeded with the differential gene  expression analysis  as a differential gene expression  analysis could be performed  among two sets of samples we performed  the analysis  in three further groups one  control and infected human bronchial  organize  to study the gene expressions while the  human bronchial organize is infected  secondly the control and treated human  bronchial organize  to see whether we could apply it as a  method to study  the side effect of our drug  thirdly we analyzed the infected and  treated human bronchial organize  in order to see the significant gene  expression throughout the treatment  from our differential gene expression  analysis between control and infected  human bronchial organoids  we could not witness any vital influence  of  different version of human reference  genome  the dendrogram looks similar in both  heat maps  only some of the gene were differently  arranged  on their rows volcano plot is  also comparable however  there is a notable difference in gene  expressions  between control and infected organoids  the differential gene expression  analysis between control  and treated human bronchial organize  also did not  show any notable influences of the  reference genome  the endogram of the heat maps look the  same  as a previous result there is a notable  difference in gene expression between  control and treated organites but the  differential gene expression analysis  between  infected and treated human bronchial  organize  does show us a difference in gene  expressions  which was influenced by a reference  genome  the dendrograms shows the different  groupings  depend on different genome and  there is a notable difference seen in  volcano plots  as well  moving on to the differential gene  expression analysis on  kick pathways we did not observe any  significant difference among the control  and infected organoids or  controlled or treated organoids  but there was an additional pathway  observed in differential expression  analysis  on kick pathways for reference genome  grch38  which shows the down expression in  pentose  and gluconate interconnections pathway  on treated bronchial organize it could  be  significant for the biochemical or  physiological  signaling pathway investigation of  bronchial orgonites  as an effect of chemostat treatment  as there was significant difference  noted in the heat maps  and the volcano plots of control  organized and the treated organized  the remarkable difference was expected  in their cake pathway analysis too  as mentioned in a slide we were able to  see  completely different pathways analysis  diagrams  depend on the human reference genomes  even though there is there are six kick  pathways that were  common among the both reference genomes  there were some unique pathways observed  for each reference genome  which probably important evidence for  signaling pathway studies  of this experiment those are the  important data  and visualizations from our  transcriptomics part  of this study  okay let's move on to the meta genomic  part of our research  although there isn't any clear evidence  to prove  that the control organites were not  contaminated  we could observe there's a difference in  their counts  for example the infected organized shows  some  more counts than the control organites  additionally we could observe the  absence of sas coronavirus1  which is hku1 in control  and treated samples which was but  founded in  infected organoid it is an interesting  topic to be  analyzed furthermore  as we looked into the significant genes  for the basal cell  club cells ciliated cells and goblet  cells  we could recognize that the tmpr ss2  s2 uh cc10  fgf1 ifn1  genes are very unique for the human  bronchial  as the research is all about tmp rss2  inhibitor  it is evident that the organized are the  best study model  among them for this research  about the second table we could see  the difference in tmp rss2 expressions  comparing  with infected organoids two third of  the treated organites show less tmp iss  expressions which is almost similar to  the expressions level  of those control organoids although  chemostat  shows the positive response as tmp  rss2 inhibitor we cannot conclude it  as a successful medicine for sas  coronavirus 2  because the experiment was conducted  among  three sets of organoids finally  then we come to the conclusions and  finding from our study  there are some differences noted in our  differential gene expression analysis  which was influenced by the reference  genome  especially the differences were  significant among organoids  but we were not able to choose a better  version  among them for a better data driven  research it is recommended to use both  reference genome  for a wide analysis  although we face some problem producing  a gene read count table for organized  using a reference genome  grch38 in few pipelines  we were able to investigate the  differential gene expression  analysis using the selfish method  so it is also important to try  different pipelines methods for a better  results  we were able to summarize all the  differential expression  of significant genes about 33 cake  tables  which could be a breakthrough for new  biochemical and physiological researches  about sas coronavirus 2 and human  bronchial organize  and its signaling pathway studies  further investigation on this topic may  lead us  to the invention of new pathways and  alternation  in the existing pathways as we noticed  theoretically  influencer a pathway is additional  information  for our study precisely the hsa  one six four cake pathway table  a study comparing a human bronchial  organize  and pulmonary tissue biopsy could give  us a real breakthrough  in the development of human organoids as  a drug of vaccine test models  especially it could help pharmaceutical  industries  scientists and medicine to avoid  unexpected outbreaks during their  experiment  on living test models it could also help  us to reduce  the consumption of time as the organize  could be manufactured quickly than other  living  test models thank you  finally i would like to thank for  elia and pine bio for giving us a  interesting uh program and the  opportunity to present our research  project  and uh i would like to thank pine bio  educational platform  and server platform rstudio  which helped me uh in some of the data  visualizations  and uh research institute for microbial  disease  who initiate the core research which we  chosen later on and ncbi for providing  the sra datas  and bio rxiv the preprint server for  biology  and my universities for providing us  informations on coronavirus and  my former uniclinic where i could still  access  my histology preparates  and nishi for introducing pinewood in  sri lanka  thank you  you

